<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    updatePeriodMillis is intentionally 0: Android's built-in widget update period is
    unreliable and has a 30-minute floor, so refresh scheduling is done entirely with our own
    WorkManager job (WidgetScheduler), as recommended for Glance widgets.

    widgetCategory includes keyguard (in addition to home_screen) so TipWidget is eligible for
    lock-screen/communal-hub widget pickers, not just the home screen — without it, the OS
    filters this widget out of that picker before the app is ever involved.

    On the sizes. Two mistakes have been made here in opposite directions, so both are written
    down. The original 140x90dp minimum was smaller than the card's own chrome, which is what
    made long tips clip. Correcting it to a 250x110dp floor then went too far the other way and
    the widget would no longer fit a small square slot at all.

    What's declared now is a genuinely wide range: min* is the true floor (2x2 on the standard
    70n-30 grid), maxResize* allows a 4x4 block, and targetCell* asks for a 2x2 default. The
    small default is chosen deliberately over the roomier 4x2 that reads best for a sentence:
    a widget that lands small can be dragged bigger by anyone who wants it bigger, while one
    that lands occupying half the home screen gets deleted rather than resized. TipWidget's
    SizeMode.Responsive supplies a layout built for each end of the range rather than one
    layout stretched across it.

    targetCellWidth/Height are API 31+ and draw two expected `UnusedAttribute` lint warnings
    against minSdk 26. They are kept anyway: on 31+ they let the launcher place the widget by
    grid cells directly, and on 26-30 they are ignored in favour of minWidth/minHeight, which
    describe the same floor. Both are needed to cover the whole range.
-->
<appwidget-provider xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="110dp"
    android:minHeight="110dp"
    android:minResizeWidth="110dp"
    android:minResizeHeight="110dp"
    android:maxResizeWidth="320dp"
    android:maxResizeHeight="320dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="2"
    android:targetCellHeight="2"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal|vertical"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen|keyguard"
    android:previewImage="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
    android:description="@string/widget_description" />
